{"format":1,"seq":554,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should fix pit by wrapping the api.output call in try/catch, since streaming output after an aborted session settles seems to get dropped silently. I want to check if there's a cleaner way to detect settled state rather than just catching, and I should look at pit's tests around onShellProgress and pi-durable's tool.js to understand how settled sessions are handled.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found it: `onShellProgress` calls `api.output` unguarded, so once pi-durable settles the call after a failed session, the next stdout chunk throws inside a socket handler and crashes the process. I'll check pi-durable's side next, along with pit's contributing rules and tests.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01XsPvGHtzDS7BCYRXwrsSwE","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Read pi-durable assertLive, pit contributing, tests mentioning onShellProgress\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }) => {\n  const r = await exec(`sed -n 280,312p node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-durable/dist/harness/tool.js; cd /tmp/pit; ls; sed -n 1,60p CONTRIBUTING.md 2>/dev/null | head -60; cat AGENTS.md 2>/dev/null | head -40; grep -rln \"onShellProgress\" src test 2>/dev/null | head; grep -n '\"scripts\"' -A15 package.json`, { timeoutMs: 30000 });\n  return r.stdout + r.stderr;\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":508,"cacheRead":111943,"cacheWrite":1213,"totalTokens":113666,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":213},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794610274742,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_rr2cwkxyhqaisbhlyn3i3n4ijq3cc5hik7tp4svt7dspbbjidasq","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":7803,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":